I thought I'd share this little story of an avoided YASD since, "MOVE
YOUR HANDS AWAY FROM KEYBOARD" seems to be a popular piece of advice.

... up late working on my YAFAP and casually descending deeper into the
main dungeon, no pets, with some wands and scrolls for getting away.
All of a sudden I step on a poly-trap, and voila! I lose most of my
armor to enjoy a brief period of being a black unicorn.  I change back
and continue down.  Suddenly I come upon a troll who is beating me
harshly, especially lacking any significant armor.  So, I run down some
stairs and find 2 leocrotta and a barracks of sleeping soldiers.  70 hp
with -2 AC does not go very far against leocrotta.  (Dang, they're
fast!)  So, instead of thinking, I read a scroll of teleport, and the
q's made it across the map before I could do much at all, so I read my
other scroll of teleport, finding myself in a long corridor.  Then just
to give me time to think, I read a scroll of earth!  Three mistakes,
just like that.  I decided that I needed some time to think and I went
to bed, cursing that all I had in my inventory was a bunch or "rotten"
wands of Digging...and as my hed hit the pillow I realized that those
wands weren't so very "rotten" after all.

So, when I resumed the game, I went back down, engraved 'Elbereth' with
the wands of digging and took care of the leocrotta.  Next time (I
hope) I'll engrave with the wands and simply walk back up out of
danger.  Hopefully I'll be able to remember this story next time I run
into trouble!

